ashleigh-cs: Hi team — Nimbus (trial) blocked on onboarding. They keep hitting 429s during SDK bootstrap in their embedded webview/kiosk. Demo tomorrow AM. Can we triage fast?

sam-support: Seeing a cluster of 429s from org=nimbus-trial in support logs. Error types: `preflight_init` and `refresh_token_rate`.

ashleigh-cs: Customer provided a tiny repro and timestamps. Logs: 
```
[2026-03-24T13:11:05Z] event=init org=nimbus-trial status=200
[2026-03-24T13:11:05Z] event=init org=nimbus-trial status=429 msg="preflight-burst"
[2026-03-24T13:11:05Z] event=worker.sync org=nimbus-trial status=200
[2026-03-24T13:11:06Z] event=init org=nimbus-trial status=429 msg="token_refresh"
```
They said multiple embedded views/firefox webviews instantiate at once.

matt-engineer: Pattern is classic multi-context fanout — main frame + embedded webviews + background sync all calling init at the same time. That creates parallel preflights and token grabs. SDK should dedupe but customer can't ship a change before demo.

diego-sre: Dashboards show ~850 preflight rpm for nimbus-trial at 13:11 which trips our short-window burst guard. I can apply a temporary edge coalescing rule and nudge their burst ceiling.

matt-engineer: Short-term server-side actions: 1) enable per-org request coalescing so identical preflight keys collapse; 2) increase short-window burst allowance by +350 for 6h; 3) temporarily extend ephemeral token TTL to reduce refresh frequency. Long-term client fix: BroadcastChannel/localStorage lock + singleflight Promise + jittered backoff on 429s.

sam-support: Customer approved a temporary server-side change over DM. They want the demo to proceed.

diego-sre: Applied: coalescing enabled for org=nimbus-trial, burst +350 (6h), ephemeral TTL bumped +22s. Monitoring now. infra-bot will post status.

infra-bot: action: enable-coalesce(org=nimbus-trial) -> ok; burst-increase(org=nimbus-trial) +350 expires in 6h; ephemeral-ttl(org=nimbus-trial) +22s.

redwood-ratebot: alert: org=nimbus-trial preflight spike detected (850 rpm) -> coalesce enabled, burst cap increased. Monitoring for repeat errors.

matt-engineer: Quick SDK example customers can apply after demo (cross-tab / multi-webview):
```js
// cross-context singleflight (BroadcastChannel + singleton promise)
const bc = typeof BroadcastChannel !== 'undefined' ? new BroadcastChannel('rw-init') : null;
let initPromise = null;
if (bc) {
  bc.onmessage = (e) => { if (e.data === 'init-done') initPromise = null; }
}
export function init() {
  if (initPromise) return initPromise;
  if (bc) bc.postMessage('init-start');
  initPromise = fetch('/v1/preflight').then(r => r.json()).finally(() => { if (bc) bc.postMessage('init-done'); initPromise = null; });
  return initPromise;
}
// also: cap concurrent preflights and add exponential jittered retry on 429
```

ashleigh-cs: I'll notify Nimbus that demo go-ahead, join the post-demo follow-up to help them integrate the SDK fix, and request they include a stable `x-client-debounce-key` header if they can (gateway can honor that to collapse duplicates).

sam-support: Scheduling 30m follow-up with Nimbus tomorrow. Saving these action items: 1) revert server-side temp changes after 6h, or extend if they ask; 2) PR for SDK singleflight + docs on embedded/webview integration; 3) consider default ephemeral TTL increase for small orgs if this pattern recurs.

diego-sre: Monitoring: error rate dropped to baseline after changes. Will revert in 6h unless CS asks to extend.

ashleigh-cs: Great work, thanks.
